---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service — Pick-Up"
  description="The terms governing use of the Pick-Up sports matchmaking app, including our zero-tolerance policy for objectionable content and abusive users."
  heading="Terms of Service"
  updated="July 2026"
>
  <div class="note">
    <p><strong>Zero tolerance.</strong> Pick-Up has zero tolerance for
    objectionable content and abusive users. Any user who posts objectionable
    content or behaves abusively toward others will have their content removed
    and will be ejected from the App. All reports are reviewed and acted on
    within 24 hours.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
  <p>
    By downloading, installing, or using the Pick-Up application ("the App"),
    you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service ("Terms"). If you do not
    agree to these Terms, do not use the App.
  </p>
  <p>These Terms apply to all users of the App, regardless of how they access it.</p>

  <h2>2. Age Requirement</h2>
  <p>
    You must be at least 18 years old to use Pick-Up. By using the App you
    confirm that you are 18 or older. If we become aware that a user is under
    18, their data will be deleted and their access removed.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Anonymous Accounts</h2>
  <p>
    Pick-Up does not require you to create an account, provide an email address,
    or submit any personal identifying information. You are assigned an
    anonymous identifier automatically when you first open the App.
  </p>
  <p>
    You may optionally set a nickname that is visible to other players in group
    chats. This nickname is not verified and should not include personal
    information you wish to keep private.
  </p>

  <h2>4. How the App Works</h2>
  <p>
    Pick-Up allows users to search for other players interested in the same
    sport in a given geographic area. When players are found searching in
    overlapping areas, they are automatically placed into a temporary group
    chat. Group chats expire after 48 hours.
  </p>
  <p>
    Pick-Up does not organise, host, or supervise any sporting events. We
    provide a communication tool only. Any arrangements made through the App —
    including where, when, and with whom you play — are made entirely at your
    own discretion.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Acceptable Use — Zero Tolerance</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>There is no tolerance for objectionable content or abusive users on
    Pick-Up.</strong> Posting objectionable content or behaving abusively will
    result in the removal of that content and the ejection of the user
    responsible.
  </p>
  <p>You agree not to use the App to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Harass, threaten, bully, or intimidate other users</li>
    <li>Post or send content that is hateful, discriminatory, obscene, sexually explicit, violent, or otherwise objectionable</li>
    <li>Solicit romantic or sexual contact. Pick-Up is for organising sports and activities only</li>
    <li>Spam other users or send unsolicited promotional messages</li>
    <li>Impersonate other users or any person</li>
    <li>Attempt to manipulate or cheat the matching system</li>
    <li>Use the App for any unlawful purpose</li>
    <li>Attempt to gain unauthorised access to any part of the App or its infrastructure</li>
    <li>Transmit viruses, malware, or other harmful code</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Moderation, Reporting, and Blocking</h2>
  <p>The App provides the following tools, available to every user:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Report</strong> — flag objectionable content or an abusive user from any group chat.</li>
    <li><strong>Block</strong> — block any user. A blocked user cannot message you, and you will not be matched with them again.</li>
    <li><strong>Delete</strong> — remove any message you have sent, immediately.</li>
    <li><strong>Leave</strong> — exit any group chat at any time.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We review every report and act within 24 hours by removing the offending
    content and ejecting the user who provided it. Additional action may include:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Temporary suspension of messaging</li>
    <li>Permanent suspension of messaging</li>
    <li>Permanent removal of the user's account and access</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We reserve the right to take action against any account at our sole
    discretion if we believe these Terms have been violated. Moderation
    decisions are final.
  </p>
  <p>
    To report a concern outside the App, contact
    <a href="mailto:PickUpHelp@proton.me">PickUpHelp@proton.me</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Location Data</h2>
  <p>
    Pick-Up requests access to your device's location solely to enable the
    sports-matching feature. Your location is used only while you have an active
    search running and is not stored permanently on our servers after your
    search is complete or cancelled.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Your location is never displayed to other users.</strong> The map and
    search radius shown in the App are visible only to you, on your own device.
    No other user can see your location, at any time or at any level of
    precision.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not sell, share, or use your location data for advertising targeting.
    For full details, see our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    Pick-Up is free to use. To support the App, we display banner advertisements
    through Google AdMob. A banner ad appears at the top of the screen while you
    use the App. It does not require any action on your part, does not interrupt
    your use of the App, and is not tied to unlocking any feature.
  </p>
  <p>
    Google AdMob may use your device's advertising identifier to serve and
    measure these ads, in accordance with Google's own privacy policies. You can
    opt out of personalised advertising through your device settings.
  </p>

  <h2>9. User-Generated Content</h2>
  <p>
    Messages sent in group chats are user-generated content. You are solely
    responsible for everything you send. Group chat messages are automatically
    deleted 48 hours after the chat is created, and you may delete any message
    you have sent at any time.
  </p>
  <p>
    Content is filtered for objectionable language, and users may report anything
    that passes the filter. By sending a message in the App, you grant Pick-Up a
    limited licence to store and transmit that content for the purpose of
    delivering it to other participants in the same group chat, and to retain it
    where necessary for moderation.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
  <p>
    The App is provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties of any
    kind, either express or implied. We do not warrant that the App will be
    uninterrupted, error-free, or free of harmful components.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not guarantee that you will be matched with other players. The
    availability of matches depends entirely on the number of other users
    searching in your area at the same time.
  </p>
  <p>
    Pick-Up is not responsible for the conduct of users you meet through the
    App. Any in-person interactions are undertaken at your own risk. Always
    exercise personal safety precautions when meeting people you do not know.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Limitation of Liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, Pick-Up and its
    developers shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special,
    consequential, or punitive damages arising from your use of the App,
    including but not limited to personal injury, property damage, or loss of
    data.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our total liability to you for any claim arising from use of the App shall
    not exceed the amount you paid to use the App in the 12 months preceding the
    claim (which, for a free app, is zero).
  </p>

  <h2>12. Intellectual Property</h2>
  <p>
    The App, including its name, logo, design, and code, is the intellectual
    property of the developer. You may not copy, modify, distribute, or
    reverse-engineer any part of the App without prior written permission.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Changes to These Terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these Terms from time to time. When we do, we will update the
    "Last updated" date at the top of this page. Continued use of the App after
    changes are posted constitutes acceptance of the updated Terms.
  </p>
  <p>
    For significant changes we will make reasonable efforts to notify users
    through the App.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Governing Law</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms are governed by the laws of the Province of Ontario, Canada,
    without regard to its conflict of law provisions. Any disputes arising from
    these Terms shall be resolved in the courts of Ontario, Canada.
  </p>

  <h2>15. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    If you have questions about these Terms or wish to report a concern, contact
    us at <a href="mailto:PickUpHelp@proton.me">PickUpHelp@proton.me</a>. We
    respond to all reports of objectionable content or abusive behaviour within
    24 hours.
  </p>
  <p>
    To report a user within the App, open any group chat, tap the ⋮ menu, and
    choose "Report a player." To block a user, tap the ⋮ menu and choose "Block
    player."
  </p>
</LegalLayout>